  "what_this_answers": "whether selective recompilation equals a full rebuild across the change space rather than across one corpus. Ground truth is the full rebuild, computed independently of the plan, so neither direction of error can hide: a missed rebuild is a stale artifact escaping and an extra rebuild is wasted work.",
  "what_this_is_not": "real data. The documents are generated, so this says nothing about real change distributions -- the corpora do that. It says the mechanism is correct on change classes the corpora happen not to contain, which is precisely what a corpus cannot say."
